{
  "info": {
    "name": "Sarfees — Women-Only (§7 rules, female-first cascade, male fallback)",
    "description": "Proves every women-only rule end to end through the natural matching flow.\n\n## What it asserts\n1. **Guards** — a male passenger cannot book women-only (403); a male driver cannot go online as a women-only driver (403).\n2. **Group isolation** — two women's women-only requests bundle into ONE `womenOnly` group; a man's regular request on the same corridor and slot lands in a SEPARATE group.\n3. **Female-first cascade** — with a male driver standing AT the pickup and a female driver 3 km away, the offer goes to the female driver.\n4. **Male fallback (§9.4, optional folder)** — with no female driver online, the male driver gets the offer as last resort, and each passenger receives the `women_only_male_driver_fallback` notification (free cancel).\n\n## How the timing works\nBookings target the next quarter-hour slot ≥ 31 min out (pre-request script). The group freezes and cascades when the slot crosses T-30 — between ~1 and ~15 min after booking. RE-RUN the poll request every ~30 s until it passes; the offer countdown is 30 s, so accept immediately.\n\n## Cast\nPassengers: Lina `790000002` (F), Dana `790000004` (F), Ahmad `790000001` (M) — mock OTP `1234`.\nDrivers: Rania `770000005` (female), Omar `770000002` (male). Admin `admin@sarfees.com`.\n\n## Prereqs\n- Backend with the §9.4 fallback fix (PR #43) deployed.\n- No leftover live requests for the cast (folder 6 cleans up after itself).\n- ⚠️ If a real driver app / emulator is logged in as a test driver, its GPS pings overwrite the activation coords every ~10 s — an emulator on default GPS (Mountain View) silently excludes that driver from matching. Set emulator GPS to Amman or log it out.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
